     constitution Articles I–III and VI, and each agent in .claude/agents/ carries the same
     block. The constitution is the AUTHORITATIVE copy; amending it means re-syncing this
     block and the agents' blocks in the SAME commit (the mirror rule). -->

- **I — [DOMAIN INVARIANT]**: [the rule that IS the product. EXAMPLE: "business objects are
  registered in metadata and read at runtime — never hardcoded as structs."]
- **II — [SAFETY INVARIANT]**: [the rule whose violation is a breach, not a bug. EXAMPLE
  (multi-tenant web): "every transactional query filters `tenant_id` — no exceptions, admin
  included; dynamic queries are parameterized, never concatenated." Or `N/A — <reason>` if the
  constitution says so.]
- **III — [ARCHITECTURE SHAPE]**: [LAYER] → [LAYER] → [LAYER]; [one-line forbidden coupling,
  EXAMPLE: "no queries in the transport layer"]. Detail:
  [`rules/architecture.md`](rules/architecture.md).
- **VI — Gates and independent acceptance**: "done" = `./gates/run-chain.sh` green — never a
  claim, mine included. Tests first: a failing test before the code it proves. Each feature is
  accepted by [ACCEPTOR — someone other than the builder] running its `quickstart.md`,
  recorded in `specs/<id>/acceptance.md`[, as a non-privileged account — keep this clause only
  where the product has an authorization boundary] ([GATES §3](../gates/GATES.md)).

## Dev commands (run from `[REPO_ROOT_OR_SUBDIR]`)

A command that feature 001 has not wired yet reads `TBD — wired by
specs/001-[walking-skeleton]`; never invent one before the code it runs exists. The format,
static, test and build rows are the commands `gates/chain.conf` runs in those slots: change
both in one commit (`./gates/run-chain.sh --list` shows what the chain runs).

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Format (check mode) | `[FORMAT_CHECK_COMMAND]` |
| Static analysis | `[LINT_COMMAND]` |
| Test | `[TEST_COMMAND]` — prints how many tests ran |
| Build | `[BUILD_COMMAND]` |
| Run locally | `[RUN_COMMAND]` |
| Full gate chain | `./gates/run-chain.sh` (`--list` shows each slot) — ritual in [`rules/workflow.md`](rules/workflow.md) |

## The flow — one line

Every feature is one directory, `specs/<id>/`: `/speckit-specify` → `/speckit-clarify` →
`/speckit-plan` → `/speckit-tasks` → `/speckit-analyze` → `/speckit-implement` →
`/speckit-converge` ([SPEC-FLOW](../model/SPEC-FLOW.md)). **HARD-GATE: no code before the
spec's frontmatter says `status: approved`, with `approved_by` and `approved_on`.** The
`spec-first` and `plan-and-tdd` skills are the discipline inside `/speckit-specify` and
`/speckit-implement`, never a second way in. Not a feature — a bug in shipped behaviour, a
hotfix, a refactor, a spike, a release? It has a lane:
[NON-FEATURE-WORK](../model/NON-FEATURE-WORK.md).

## The gate chain — one line

`./gates/run-chain.sh` runs the slots in `gates/chain.conf` in order — format → static → test →
build → orphan-endpoints → acceptance → doc-sync → spec-approval → spec-numbers — and stops at
the first red. No commit on red, no exceptions ([GATES](../gates/GATES.md)). A `TODO` slot is
red until feature 001 wires it; an `NA: <reason>` slot prints its reason every run. The
per-feature acceptance run is not a chain slot: it is the `acceptance.md` record that the
`spec-approval` slot checks.

## When code and spec disagree

Find out which one moved. If the spec states intended behaviour the code does not deliver, the
code is wrong: record a new task (converge). If the code reflects a deliberate, owner-approved
change the spec never recorded, fix the spec with the correction marked (≠old) and a dated
Clarifications entry. If you cannot tell, ask the owner.

## The guard

`.claude/hooks/check-careful.py`, registered in `.claude/settings.json`, asks before destructive
commands and denies the ones nothing undoes — including any change to its own files and to the
gate scripts ([careful](skills/careful/SKILL.md)). Its `careful.json` is adapted before
`adopt.py --register-guard`; after that the guard denies an agent's edit to it, and a human
makes the change. A deny is a wall: report it to the owner, never route around it. If
`factory/` is empty, run `git submodule update --init` before anything else — every link into
it is dead until then.

## Roles and lazy-loaded detail

Roles in `.claude/agents/`: `requirement-researcher` · `task-orchestra` · `tech-lead-review` ·
`tester-e2e`. Each carries an INVARIANTS block mirroring the section above.

Rules in `.claude/rules/`: [`architecture`](rules/architecture.md) · [`data`](rules/data.md) ·
[`api-conventions`](rules/api-conventions.md) · [`workflow`](rules/workflow.md). The adopt.py
profile may have left some out (a CLI has no API conventions); a rule it dropped shows here as
plain text — delete its name. Each rule scopes itself with a `paths:` key (Claude Code's) in
frontmatter that opens on line 1; a rule without one loads in every session, and so does a
rule whose frontmatter does not open on line 1 (HARNESS.md §3).
